---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PRODUCT_NAME, BRAND, CONTACT_EMAIL, MAILTO, CF_WEB_ANALYTICS_TOKEN, CF_WEB_ANALYTICS_ON } from '../config/brand';
---
<Base title={`Privacy | ${BRAND}`} description={`No account = we store nothing. How ${PRODUCT_NAME} and this site handle your files: read in your browser, never uploaded.`} path="/privacy" ogImage="/og/hub.png" section="hub" crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy' }]}>
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lead"><strong>Short version:</strong> No account = we store nothing. Your spreadsheet is read in your browser and never sent to us.</p>
      <h2>{PRODUCT_NAME} without an account (Try)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The file you import is read in your browser. It is not uploaded.</li>
        <li>Your lab lives only in that browser tab. Close the tab and it's gone; we never had a copy.</li>
        <li>Try sets no cookies, uses no browser storage and makes no requests to third-party servers. You can download your lab as a file and import it again later.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>{CF_WEB_ANALYTICS_ON || CF_WEB_ANALYTICS_TOKEN ? <>We count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics: no cookies, no browser storage, no fingerprinting. It records the page, the referring site, the country and the device type, and we only see totals. No other analytics, no ads, and no other third-party scripts except Cloudflare's bot check on the waitlist form.</> : <>No analytics, no cookies, no ads and no third-party scripts (one exception: Cloudflare's bot check on the waitlist form, below).</>} The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages; Cloudflare receives your IP address to deliver and protect the pages, as described in Cloudflare's privacy policy.</li>
        <li>The calculators run in your browser. If you pick a currency, an electricity price, calculator inputs or the theme (Auto, Dark, Bright), your browser remembers it on your device. We don't receive it.</li>
        <li>If you e-mail us to hear when Account and Pro open, we use your address for that one reply and then delete it.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>The waitlist</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>If you join the waitlist we store your e-mail address, the product you picked, the optional note about your rack, where you came from (the <code>?src</code> in the link, for example <code>yt</code>) and your browser's user-agent string, plus a one-way hash of your IP address that only serves to limit spam (five tries per hour).</li>
        <li>A Cloudflare Turnstile check on the form tells people from bots. It runs Cloudflare's script on that page only.</li>
        <li>We use the address for one e-mail when the self-serve Try opens. We don't share it and we don't add it to any other list. Ask us at <a href={MAILTO}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we delete it.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>With an Account (when available)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We store your lab, its history and your account details so you can come back to them. Ask us at <a href={MAILTO}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we delete your lab or your account.</li>
        <li>Payments will be handled by our payment provider. We never see your card number.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>rack-density.com, {PRODUCT_NAME} and DC Sim are run by Mustard Seed Solutions (Malta, <a href="https://mustardseedmt.com" rel="noopener">mustardseedmt.com</a>), which is responsible for the data described here. Sensaka and {BRAND} are its brands. Questions: <a href={MAILTO}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
      <p class="small muted">Last updated: 15 October 2026 (visit counting added)</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
